      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the remainder when the sum of the first five primes is divided by the sixth prime, we first need to determine the values of each prime number.\n\n1. First Prime: 2\n2. Second Prime: 3\n3. Third Prime: 5\n4. Fourth Prime: 7\n5. Fifth Prime: 11\n\nNow, let's find the sum of these prime numbers:\n\nFirst, we add all the primes:\n\n\\[\n2 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 11\n\\]\n\nDoing the calculation step-by-step:\n\n\\[\n2 + 3 = 5\n\\]\n\n\\[\n5 + 5 = 10\n\\]\n\n\\[\n10 + 7 = 17\n\\]\n\n\\[\n17 + 11 = 28\n\\]\n\nThe sum of the first five primes is 28. Next, we need to find the remainder when 28 is divided by the sixth prime, which is 13.\n\nWe perform the division:\n\n\\[\n28 \\div 13 = 2 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 10\n\\]\n\nHence,\n\n\\[\n28 = 13 \\times 2 + 10\n\\]\n\nThe remainder is 10. Therefore, the remainder when the sum of the first five primes is divided by the sixth prime is \\boxed{10}.",
